CAESAR Desktop - licensing
==========================

The source code of CAESAR Desktop is licensed under the MIT License below,
with the following exceptions, which are licensed under the GNU Affero
General Public License version 3 only (AGPL-3.0-only):

  - morse/deepcw/            the DeepCW CW decoding model (model.onnx,
                             model.onnx.json), from
                             https://github.com/e04/deepcw-engine
  - morse/deepcw_engine.py   a Python port of the deepcw-engine reference
                             implementation

The full text of the AGPL-3.0 is in morse/deepcw/LICENSE.

Because the CW decoder runs as part of the application, the built
application (the AppImage and Windows executables published on the
Releases page, and any other build that includes the files above) is a
combined work and is distributed under the terms of AGPL-3.0-only. Its
complete corresponding source code is this repository at the release tag
matching the version (for example, v1.2.0 for version 1.2.0):
https://github.com/ra0sms/caesar-client-desktop

The MIT-licensed files may still be used on their own under the MIT
License.

